CORE gcc-only no-new-smt
main.c
--arch arm --unwind 2 --no-unwinding-assertions
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
approximating inline assembly
--
The AArch32 inline assembly in main.c is interpreted exactly: if CBMC
approximated any statement, the assertions, which check values observed with
an emulator (Unicorn, and qemu-arm for A32 code compiled by GCC and Clang),
would fail. A store-exclusive may fail spuriously, so the retry loops of
load-exclusive/store-exclusive sequences are bounded; the executions that
retry more often reach the same states.
